\begin{figure}[hbt] % between [] you put options e.g. ht = here top
% \hspace*{-0.5cm}
 %\hspace*{-2cm}
\centering
%\rule{12.8cm}{7.2cm}
%\setlength{\abovecaptionskip}{5pt}
\makebox[\textwidth]{\includegraphics[width=0.7\paperwidth]{figure/NplRatios2-1}}
\vspace{-1cm}}
%\caption{NPL(\%) ratios per country: Households, Non-Financial Corporations \& Financial Corporations}
\caption{NPL per Country}
\label{NplRatios2}
 \vspace*{-3mm}
\end{figure}
Figure \ref{NplRatios2} represents the NPL distribution per bank's country of origin. At country level, Greece and Cyprus  stand out as they have the highest NPL ratios for all exposure types. Other countries with heightened NPL from non-financial corporations are Portugal and Slovenia followed by Spain and Italy. For the case of  NPL from financial corporations, Ireland and Portugal show  comparatively  the highest levels. In general, Figure \ref{NplRatios2} illustrates some differences in NPL between EU member states in line with the often recognized core-periphery structure in the distribution of NPL in the European Union.

